diff --git a/index.html b/index.html
--- a/index.html
+++ b/index.html
@@ -0,0 +1,37 @@
+<!DOCTYPE html>
+<html lang="en">
+<head>
+  <meta charset="UTF-8">
+  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
+  <title>Visually Stable Mixed Fonts &amp; Independent Theme Proportions</title>
+  <link rel="stylesheet" href="styles.css">
+</head>
+<body>
+  <main>
+    <header>
+      <h1>Normalized Typography Proportions</h1>
+      <p>Demonstrating visual height normalization across mixed font families and independent theme containers using modern CSS.</p>
+    </header>
+
+    <section id="mixed-fonts-container" class="typography-card" aria-labelledby="mixed-fonts-heading">
+      <h2 id="mixed-fonts-heading">Mixed Font Families Container</h2>
+      <p>
+        When mixing regular body copy with inline code snippets like <code>const visualScale = "from-font";</code> or <code>font-size-adjust: from-font</code>, differences in lowercase x-height between proportional and monospace typefaces can make inline code appear disproportionately small or jarring.
+      </p>
+      <p>
+        By applying <code>font-size-adjust: from-font</code> on <code>#mixed-fonts-container</code>, the browser automatically extracts the primary font's x-height aspect ratio and scales nested <code>&lt;code&gt;</code> elements to match the visual height of the surrounding text seamlessly.
+      </p>
+    </section>
+
+    <section id="independent-theme-container" class="typography-card" aria-labelledby="independent-theme-heading">
+      <h2 id="independent-theme-heading">Independent Theme Container</h2>
+      <p>
+        This separate container uses a serif typeface (<code>Times New Roman</code> / <code>Georgia</code>) to represent an independent editorial theme. Normally, switching to a serif font at the same nominal <code>font-size</code> produces noticeably smaller lowercase characters compared to a high-x-height sans-serif like Verdana.
+      </p>
+      <p>
+        Applying a specific numeric metric override (<code>font-size-adjust: 0.51</code>) locks down the container's x-height aspect ratio directly, ensuring consistent visual proportions and legibility without relying on parent font inheritance.
+      </p>
+    </section>
+  </main>
+</body>
+</html>
